ettings":{"title":"Benefits of Utilizing AI in Data Center Ops","title_color":"#FFFFFF","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":30,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"700","typography_line_height_mobile":{"unit":"em","size":1.5,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"5d161b5","elType":"widget","settings":{"space_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"a6b87f3","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Reapmind Innovations / 20th July 2024</p>","text_color":"#FFFFFF","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_size_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":14.6,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"},{"id":"d868ead","elType":"widget","settings":{"space_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":251,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"117522d","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"ed010e4","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"35f9a43","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"5fdeed5","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>What if Power of AI in Data Center Operation could predict and prevent problems before they even happened? What if it could optimize its energy use, saving you money and reducing your carbon footprint? What if it could even strengthen its security, protecting your valuable data? This isn’t the stuff of science fiction; it’s the reality that <a href="https://reapmind.com/artificial-intelligence-future-of-your-business/">artificial intelligence</a> (AI) is bringing to data centers today. AI is revolutionizing how we manage these critical facilities, promising unprecedented levels of efficiency, reliability, and security.</p>
<p>In this blog, we’ll delve into the specifics of how AI is revolutionizing<a href="https://www.microland.com/digital/hybrid-cloud-services/datacenter-management"> data center management</a>, from predictive maintenance and automated optimization to advanced security measures and beyond. We’ll explore real-world examples of how AI is already transforming data centers, making them smarter, more efficient, and more resilient than ever before. Whether you’re a data center operator, an IT professional, or simply curious about the future of technology, this blog will shed light on the remarkable potential of AI to reshape the very foundations of our digital world.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"1e27f6e","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"d529912","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"ef5c4c4","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Introduction: The Rise of the Intelligent Data Center","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_font_weight":"600","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"e3b9f5b","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"5a8256a","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Data centers, the beating heart of the digital age, are undergoing a revolution. No longer simply repositories of vast information, they’re evolving into intelligent entities. This transformation is driven by a powerful force: artificial intelligence (AI).</p>
<p>Traditionally, data centers have been plagued by challenges like unexpected equipment failures, soaring energy costs, and the constant threat of <a href="https://www.ibm.com/topics/cyber-attack">cyberattacks</a>. These issues can lead to costly downtime, operational inefficiencies, and potential data breaches. However, the advent of AI is fundamentally changing this landscape.</p>
<p>AI is infusing data centers with a new level of intelligence, allowing them to predict and prevent problems before they occur, optimize energy use with remarkable precision, and bolster security to unprecedented levels. This shift towards proactive, self-optimizing, and secure data centers is a paradigm shift in how we manage and operate these critical facilities.</p>
<p>In this era of the intelligent data center, AI algorithms are continuously analyzing vast streams of data from sensors, logs, and other sources. They’re identifying patterns, detecting anomalies, and making real-time adjustments to ensure optimal performance, reliability, and security. This not only reduces costs and minimizes downtime but also enables data centers to become more sustainable and environmentally friendly.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"ffdb8c8","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"712fcfa","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"38f3d96","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance: A Deep Dive into Preventing Data Center Disruptions","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"4f781a0","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"e329232","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>The traditional approach to data center maintenance, often referred to as “<a href="https://www.ibm.com/topics/reactive-maintenance">reactive maintenance</a>,” has long been the standard. This approach involves monitoring equipment and responding to failures as they occur. While this method may seem straightforward, it is fraught with inefficiencies and hidden costs. Unexpected downtime, expensive emergency repairs, premature equipment replacement, and the constant need for reactive troubleshooting are just a few of the challenges faced by data center operators who rely on reactive maintenance.</p>
<p>Enter AI-powered predictive maintenance, a revolutionary approach that leverages the power of artificial intelligence and machine learning to transform how data centers are managed. By analyzing vast amounts of data collected from sensors and logs, AI algorithms can identify subtle patterns and anomalies that often precede equipment failures. This enables data center operators to take proactive measures, addressing potential issues before they escalate into costly disruptions.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"512cf5f","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"012d216","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"bd728bd","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"How AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance Works","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"2f1d932","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"2f83437","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p><strong><img class="aligncenter wp-image-99501 size-full" src="https://reapmind.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Frame-13.png" alt="How AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance Works" width="1832" height="564" />Data Collection:</strong> A vast network of sensors embedded within data center equipment continuously monitors various parameters, such as temperature, vibration, humidity, power consumption, and fan speeds. This data is collected in real-time, providing a comprehensive view of the health and performance of each component.</p><p><strong>Data Aggregation and Preprocessing:</strong> The collected data is aggregated and preprocessed to ensure consistency and accuracy. This step involves cleaning the data, removing outliers, and transforming it into a format suitable for analysis.</p><p><strong>Feature Engineering:</strong> Relevant features are extracted from the preprocessed data. These features represent the key indicators of equipment health and performance, such as temperature trends, vibration frequencies, and power consumption patterns.</p><p><strong>Machine Learning Model Training:</strong> Advanced machine learning algorithms, such as neural networks or decision trees, are trained on historical data to identify patterns and correlations that indicate potential failures. These models learn from past events and become increasingly accurate at predicting future failures.</p><p><strong>Predictive Modeling:</strong> The trained models are used to analyze real-time data from the data center, generating predictions about the likelihood and timing of equipment failures. These predictions are often accompanied by confidence levels, indicating the degree of certainty in the forecast.</p><p><strong>Actionable Insights:</strong> The predictions are translated into actionable insights, such as recommended maintenance actions, optimal replacement schedules, and early warning alerts. This empowers data center operators to make informed decisions and take proactive measures to prevent failures before they occur.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"91ef8b2","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"08ecfd6","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"2fe8276","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Benefits of AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"7fb5d8b","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"d71d9b0","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>The advantages of implementing AI-powered predictive maintenance in data centers are significant and far-reaching:<img class="aligncenter wp-image-99502 size-full" src="https://reapmind.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Frame-14.png" alt="Benefits of AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance" width="1832" height="1048" /></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Reduced Downtime:</strong> By proactively addressing potential issues, AI can minimize or even eliminate unplanned downtime, ensuring continuous operation and maximizing uptime.</li><li><strong>Extended Equipment Lifespan:</strong> Early detection and targeted repairs can significantly extend the lifespan of critical equipment, optimizing the return on investment.</li><li><strong>Cost Savings:</strong> Avoiding costly emergency repairs and unplanned downtime can result in substantial cost savings, both in terms of maintenance expenses and lost revenue due to outages.</li><li><strong>Improved Resource Allocation:</strong> Maintenance teams can shift from reactive firefighting to proactive planning, focusing on optimizing maintenance schedules and improving overall efficiency.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Reliability:</strong> A proactive approach to maintenance improves the overall reliability and resilience of the data center, reducing the risk of unexpected disruptions and ensuring a more stable operating environment.</li></ul>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"df1d4ee","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"2c5d984","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"34468f8","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Real-World Applications of AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance in Data Centers","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_line_height":{"unit":"em","size":1.3,"sizes":[]},"typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"488d12a","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"122a7ed","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>The transformative power of AI-powered predictive maintenance isn’t just theoretical; it’s already making a tangible impact in real-world data centers. Leading technology companies and industrial giants alike are leveraging AI to optimize their operations, reduce costs, and enhance the reliability of their critical infrastructure. Here are some notable examples:<img class="aligncenter wp-image-99504 size-full" src="https://reapmind.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Frame-15.png" alt="Real-World Applications of AI-Powered Predictive Maintenance in Data Centers" width="1832" height="719" /></p><h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Google" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>Google:</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Google operates massive data centers that consume enormous amounts of energy. Cooling system failures can lead to significant downtime and energy waste.</li><li><strong>AI Solution:</strong> Google developed an AI-powered system that analyzes data from thousands of sensors in its data centers. The system can predict cooling system failures up to 48 hours in advance, allowing for proactive maintenance and preventing costly outages.</li><li><strong>Impact:</strong> Google has reported a 40% reduction in cooling-related energy consumption and a significant decrease in unplanned downtime due to cooling failures.</li></ul><h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Microsoft" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>Microsoft:</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Microsoft’s data centers house a vast array of servers and networking equipment, with potential hardware failures posing a constant threat to service availability.</li><li><strong>AI Solution:</strong> Microsoft employs AI algorithms to analyze server logs and performance data, identifying patterns that indicate potential hardware failures. This allows them to proactively replace failing components before they cause disruptions.</li><li><strong>Impact:</strong> Microsoft has achieved significant cost savings by reducing hardware failures and avoiding unplanned downtime. They have also reported improved resource allocation, as maintenance teams can focus on strategic tasks rather than reactive repairs.</li></ul><h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Siemens" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>Siemens:</strong></h3><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Challenge:</strong> Siemens provides industrial equipment and services to a wide range of industries, including manufacturing, energy, and transportation. Maintaining this equipment is crucial for ensuring the smooth operation of critical infrastructure.</li><li><strong>AI Solution:</strong> Siemens uses AI to analyze sensor data from its equipment, predicting maintenance needs and optimizing maintenance schedules. This helps customers minimize downtime, reduce maintenance costs, and extend the lifespan of their equipment.</li><li><strong>Impact:</strong> Siemens has reported significant improvements in customer satisfaction, reduced maintenance costs, and increased equipment uptime due to the implementation of AI-powered predictive maintenance.</li></ul><h3 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Other_Notable_Examples" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>Other Notable Examples:</strong></h3><ul><li style="list-style-type: none;"><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Amazon Web Services (AWS):</strong> <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/console/">AWS</a> uses AI to predict storage drive failures and proactively replace them, ensuring data availability and minimizing the risk of data loss.</li><li><strong>Facebook:</strong> Facebook employs AI to analyze data from its vast network infrastructure, predicting and preventing network outages that could impact billions of users.</li><li><strong>General Electric (GE):</strong> GE uses AI to predict maintenance needs for its jet engines, wind turbines, and other industrial equipment, optimizing maintenance schedules and reducing downtime.</li></ul></li></ul>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"2b2610e","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"0ef7106","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"625c1a8","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"The Energy Challenge: Power-Hungry Data Centers","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"34963eb","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"848817a","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Data centers are notorious energy hogs. They consume vast amounts of electricity to power servers, storage devices, and networking equipment, as well as to cool these components to prevent overheating. This energy consumption not only contributes to significant operating costs but also has a substantial environmental impact, with data centers accounting for a growing portion of global carbon emissions.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"97c5bd5","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"aba141a","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"0f09ba6","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"AI’s Role in Optimization: Smarter Energy Management","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"00ff654","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"bd8b956","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>Artificial intelligence (AI) offers a transformative solution to this energy challenge. By leveraging AI algorithms, data centers can optimize energy consumption in several key areas:<img class="aligncenter wp-image-99505 size-full" src="https://reapmind.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Frame-16-1.png" alt="AI’s Role in Optimization: Smarter Energy Management" width="1832" height="1048" /></p><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Cooling:</strong> AI can analyze real-time data from temperature sensors and adjust cooling systems accordingly. This ensures that cooling is provided only where and when it’s needed, minimizing energy waste.</li><li><strong>Power Distribution:</strong> AI can monitor power usage patterns and dynamically allocate power resources to where they’re most needed. This prevents overprovisioning and ensures that energy is not wasted on idle equipment.</li><li><strong>Workload Management:</strong> AI can analyze workload patterns and distribute tasks across servers in a way that optimizes energy efficiency. This can involve shifting workloads to servers that are already running or consolidating workloads onto fewer servers during periods of low demand.</li></ul>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"4b9d447","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"a8ce1b1","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"909fe4e","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Potential Savings: A Significant Impact","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600","typography_letter_spacing":{"unit":"px","size":0.3,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"9ea82f4","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"2f102a4","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>The potential energy and cost savings achievable through AI-driven optimization are substantial. Studies have shown that AI can reduce data center energy consumption by up to 40%. This translates to significant cost savings for data center operators, as well as a reduced environmental impact.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="Additional_Benefits_More_than_Just_Energy_Savings" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>Additional Benefits: More than Just Energy Savings</strong></h2>
<p>Energy optimization isn’t just about reducing costs and carbon emissions. It also has a positive impact on equipment lifespan. By operating equipment at optimal temperatures and minimizing stress, AI can help extend the life of servers and other components. This further reduces costs and contributes to a more sustainable data center.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading"><span id="How_ReapMind_empower_you_in_AI_driven_powerful_solutions" class="ez-toc-section"></span><strong>How ReapMind empower you in AI driven powerful solutions?</strong></h2>
<p>Artificial intelligence (AI) isn’t just about self-driving cars or <a href="https://reapmind.com/chatbots-development/">chatbots</a> anymore; it’s transforming how data centers operate. By harnessing the power of AI, data center managers can proactively address challenges that have long plagued these critical facilities. AI algorithms can analyze vast amounts of data from sensors and logs, predicting equipment failures before they happen, optimizing energy consumption to save costs and reduce environmental impact, and strengthening security measures to protect valuable data.</p>
<p>Partnering with a company like ReapMind, specializing in AI-driven solutions, can unlock the full potential of AI in your data center. They can tailor AI models to your specific needs, whether it’s predictive maintenance, energy optimization, or security enhancement. <a href="https://reapmind.com/">ReapMind</a>‘s expertise in data analytics, machine learning, and AI algorithms can help you transform your data center into a more efficient, reliable, and secure operation.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"7c9d279","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"bdeeec8","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"401ae10","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"Conclusion","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","header_size":"p","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"2db35da","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"15731af","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p>The fusion of artificial intelligence (AI) and data centers is rewriting the rules of efficiency, reliability, and security. AI is no longer a futuristic concept; it’s a practical tool transforming how these critical hubs operate. From predicting failures before they happen to optimizing energy use and fortifying security, AI is making data centers smarter, greener, and more resilient. The message is clear: Embrace AI, and propel your data center into a future where innovation and efficiency reign supreme.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true},{"id":"e0347ad","elType":"section","settings":[],"elements":[{"id":"4db8886","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null},"elements":[{"id":"0d54cf4","elType":"widget","settings":{"title":"FAQ’s","typography_typography":"custom","typography_font_family":"Poppins","title_color":"#012D50","header_size":"p","typography_font_size":{"unit":"px","size":28,"sizes":[]},"typography_font_weight":"600"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"heading"},{"id":"fe7b7f7","elType":"widget","settings":{"space":{"unit":"px","size":20,"sizes":[]}},"elements":[],"widgetType":"spacer"},{"id":"d75d304","elType":"widget","settings":{"editor":"<p><strong>What is AI-powered predictive maintenance?</strong></p>
<p>AI-powered predictive maintenance uses machine learning algorithms to analyze data from sensors and logs within your data center. This helps predict potential equipment failures before they happen, allowing for proactive maintenance and preventing costly downtime.</p>
<p><strong>How does AI optimize energy consumption in data centers?</strong></p>
<p>AI algorithms dynamically adjust cooling systems, power distribution, and workload management based on real-time data. This ensures optimal energy use, reduces waste, and lowers your energy bills.</p>
<p><strong>Can AI enhance data center security?</strong></p>
<p>Absolutely! AI can analyze network traffic, user behavior, and system logs to detect anomalies and potential security threats. This allows for quicker response times and stronger defenses against cyberattacks.</p>
<p><strong>What are the main benefits of using AI in data center operations?</strong></p>
<p>The key benefits include:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Reduced downtime due to predictive maintenance</li>
<li>Increased equipment lifespan</li>
<li>Significant energy cost savings</li>
<li>Enhanced security and threat detection</li>
<li>Improved operational efficiency through automation</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Is AI going to replace human jobs in data centers?</strong></p>
<p>No. While AI automates certain tasks, it also creates new roles for IT professionals. Humans are still needed for strategic decision-making, complex problem-solving, and managing the overall AI systems.</p>
<p><strong>Is AI implementation in data centers expensive?</strong></p>
<p>The initial investment may seem significant, but the long-term cost savings from reduced downtime, energy efficiency, and improved operations often outweigh the upfront costs.</p>"},"elements":[],"widgetType":"text-editor"}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":true}],"isInner":false},{"id":"a3504b3","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":33,"_inline_size":23.171,"hide_tablet":"hidden-tablet","hide_mobile":"hidden-mobile"},"elements":[{"id":"c5abbce","elType":"section","settings":{"height_inner":"min-height","sticky":"top","sticky_offset":100,"sticky_effects_offset":100,"sticky_parent":"yes","the7_sticky_row_overlap":"yes","the7_hide_on_sticky_effect":"show"},"elements":[{"id":"e820f8a","elType":"column","settings":{"_column_size":100,"_inline_size":null,"css_classes":"stickForm","hide_tablet":"hidden-tablet","custom_css":".stickForm{
